 "cards": [
  {
   "dot": "emerald",
   "title": "Four questions kept separate",
   "items": [
    "Which relationship is being measured: linear, rank, tail, lead-lag or partial",
    "How to estimate it from irregular ticks without the Epps bias",
    "How much of the matrix is noise, given q = variables / observations",
    "How to combine many sensors into one signal"
   ]
  },
  {
   "dot": "violet",
   "title": "One formula in two fields",
   "items": [
    "Optimal array weights (Capon 1969) and minimum-variance portfolio weights (Markowitz 1952) are the same expression",
    "Diagonal loading in beamforming is linear shrinkage (Ledoit and Wolf 2004)",
    "The seismic denoiser and the Spanish solar project import these modules"
   ]
  },
